From: LuneOS port <webos-ports@webos-ports.org>
Subject: [PATCH] start: retry legacy clone without CLONE_PIDFD on EINVAL

The clone3() fallback for pre-5.3 kernels calls legacy clone() with
CLONE_PIDFD still set, on the assumption that legacy clone silently
ignores unknown flags. On arm32 4.14 (MT6739) it does not: the kernel
rejects the flag with EINVAL and the container never starts:

  clone3({...}, 88)  = -1 ENOSYS
  clone3({...}, 64)  = -1 ENOSYS
  clone(child_stack=NULL, flags=CLONE_PIDFD|CLONE_NEWNS|CLONE_NEWUTS|
        CLONE_NEWIPC|CLONE_NEWPID|SIGCHLD, ...) = -1 EINVAL

Retry without CLONE_PIDFD, the same escape the function already has for
arm64. handler->pidfd stays negative, so the existing
"if (handler->pidfd < 0) clone_flags &= ~CLONE_PIDFD" cleanup path and
lxc_can_use_pidfd() handle the rest.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [lxc 4.0 is EOL upstream]
---
--- a/src/lxc/start.c
+++ b/src/lxc/start.c
@@ -1735,6 +1735,15 @@
 			handler->pid = lxc_raw_legacy_clone(handler->clone_flags & ~CLONE_PIDFD, NULL);
 		#else
 			handler->pid = lxc_raw_legacy_clone(handler->clone_flags, &handler->pidfd);
+			/*
+			 * Not every pre-pidfd kernel ignores unknown legacy
+			 * clone flags: arm32 4.14 returns EINVAL for
+			 * CLONE_PIDFD. Retry without it.
+			 */
+			if (handler->pid < 0 && errno == EINVAL) {
+				SYSTRACE("Failed legacy clone with CLONE_PIDFD, retrying without");
+				handler->pid = lxc_raw_legacy_clone(handler->clone_flags & ~CLONE_PIDFD, NULL);
+			}
 		#endif
 		}

